   *
   * Snapshots are automatically created whenever a seller edits a variant, preserving the complete state at that moment including SKU code, price, and option values. Each snapshot captures:
   * - The timestamp when the change was made
   * - The SKU code at that point in time
   * - The variant price at that point in time
   * - The complete option values configuration
   *
   * This operation supports pagination and time-based filtering to browse through the variant's edit history. Snapshots are immutable and cannot be modified or deleted, serving as authoritative records for dispute resolution. Sellers can view snapshots of their own variants to track changes over time. Snapshots remain preserved even if the variant or parent product is deleted.
   *
   * Requires proper authorization to view snapshots - typically the product owner seller or platform administrators.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param productId Unique identifier of the product (UUID format) to which the variant belongs
   * @param variantId Unique identifier of the variant (UUID format) whose snapshots are being retrieved
   * @param body Pagination and filtering criteria for retrieving variant snapshots. Supports time range filtering to view snapshots within specific periods.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor seller
   * @x-autobe-specification Query ecommerce_mall_product_variant_snapshots table filtered by product_variant_id. Join with ecommerce_mall_product_variant_snapshot_option_values to retrieve complete option value snapshots. Implement pagination with cursor-based or offset pagination. Support ordering by created_at (descending default to show newest first). Validate that the requesting user has permission to view snapshots for this variant (product owner or admin). Return summary view suitable for list display showing snapshot date, SKU code, price, and option values.
